skill: "hashtag-strategy"
sections[11]:
  - "\n"
  - "# Hashtag Strategy\n\nThe most valuable thing this skill does is correct an outdated belief. In 2026, **hashtags are not a\nreach hack** — platforms understand content directly (captions, on-screen text, audio, visuals,\nengagement), so tags now mostly **categorize** a post and **aid search**. Instagram even removed\nhashtag-following (2024) and **caps hashtags at 5** (2025), and its own head has said more tags\ndon't mean more reach.\n\nSo this skill does two jobs, in order:\n\n1. **The keyword / social-SEO layer first** — the real discovery lever. Platforms are search\n   engines now; they index your caption, on-screen text, and spoken audio.\n2. **A tight, relevant hashtag set** on top — per platform, within caps, niche over generic — plus\n   branded/campaign tags where community applies.\n\n(Full reasoning in `references/the-2026-reality.md`.)\n\n"
  - "## Step 0 — Read the foundation + the post\n\nLoad `brand-profile.md` and `audience.md`, and look at the actual content/caption being tagged. Tags\nmust match real content and the audience's real searches.\n\n"
  - "## Step 1 — Set the keyword / social-SEO layer (the real lever)\n\nPick the **primary keyword** (how the audience actually searches) + a couple of variations, and\nplace them where platforms index:\n\n- **Caption, front-loaded** (the first ~80 chars carry most weight).\n- **On-screen text** (Reels/TikTok/Shorts).\n- **Spoken audio** (video) — say the keyword aloud; on TikTok the \"triple mention\" (say + show +\n  caption) is the core ranking move.\n\nThis does more for discovery than any tag. Don't skip it to jump to hashtags.\n\n"
  - "## Step 2 — Pick a tight, relevant hashtag set per platform\n\nPer `references/platform-playbook.md`: Instagram 3–5 (hard cap 5), TikTok 3–5 as keywords, LinkedIn\n3–5 specific, X 0–2, Threads 1, Pinterest/YouTube keywords-led. Favor **mid-tier/niche tags\n(~10K–500K posts)** over mega-tags; mix topic + niche/community + (sometimes) location/branded. Vet\neach tag on its page before using (see `references/research-and-types.md`).\n\n"
  - "## Step 3 — Add branded / campaign tags where they apply\n\nFor community/UGC/tracking, design a **branded** tag (ongoing) or **campaign** tag (time-bound):\nshort, unique, unused, typo-safe, on-brand, and promoted in bio/caption/CTA. This is the one place\nhashtags still pull real weight.\n\n"
  - "## Step 4 — Rotate sets; place; publish\n\n- Build **2–4 reusable sets per pillar** and rotate by what each post is about — don't paste one\n  identical block.\n- **Placement:** caption (best for search/SEO on most platforms).\n- **Publish:** hand the post + tags to `scheduling-and-queue`. Respect the **IG 5-cap** so a post\n  isn't blocked/trimmed.\n\n"
  - "## Quality bar — self-check\n\n- Did I lead with the **keyword/SEO layer**, not hashtags?\n- Is the tag set **tight, relevant, niche/mid-tier**, and **within the platform's cap**?\n- Is it **per-platform**, not one block everywhere?\n- Did I avoid **generic mega-tags / #fyp / 30-tag dumps**?\n- Did I add a **branded/campaign tag** where community/UGC applies?\n- Are sets **rotated**, and is the expectation set **honestly** (categorize + search, not reach)?\n- **No analytics claims** WoopSocial can't back?\n\n"
  - "## Edge cases & pushback\n\n- **\"Give me 30 to go viral\"** → push back: more tags ≠ more reach; IG caps at 5; redirect to\n  keywords + content + engagement. Deliver a tight set.\n- **\"Add #fyp #viral #explore\"** → decline generic mega-tags; explain #fyp doesn't affect the FYP;\n  offer niche/mid-tier.\n- **\"Same block on every post\"** → rotate relevant sets; note copy-paste is low-effort (and frame\n  the shadowban claim accurately — unconfirmed, but relevance/rotation still wins).\n- **\"Which hashtags perform best for us?\"** → no WoopSocial analytics; point to native\n  reach-from-hashtags insights or qualitative review.\n- **Wrong platform** → don't tag X like Instagram; match the playbook.\n- **Regulated/sensitive** → avoid tags implying unverifiable claims; carry brand guardrails.\n\n"
  - "## Related skills\n\n- `brand-profile`, `audience-research` — relevance + how the audience searches.\n- `caption-writer`, `tiktok-script`, `reels-script`, `carousel-writer`, `linkedin-post-writer` —\n  where the keyword/SEO layer and tags actually live.\n- `social-seo`, `ai-search-optimization` — the deeper search/discoverability skills.\n- `trend-jacking` — riding a live tag/sound moment (vs. evergreen tags here).\n- `scheduling-and-queue` — publish with the tags in the caption.\n\n"
  - "## References\n\n- `references/the-2026-reality.md` — why hashtags ≠ reach now; what they do; the real levers; myths.\n- `references/platform-playbook.md` — per-platform counts, caps, and the real lever for each.\n- `references/research-and-types.md` — the 8 tag types, vetting, rotating sets, branded/campaign design.\n- `references/examples.md` — worked keyword+tag sets per platform, vs the old 30-tag block.\n"
